 "summary": "The new material is genuinely absent from EpsilonEridani and from Mathlib/TauCeti/Physlib, and it reuses the existing DIS kinematics where it can: hardKinematics/trueInvariants go through DisKinematics.xBj/Q2/yInel, sigmaMethod reuses SigmaMethodData.ySigma and its ySigma_eq_yInel, the shared bilinear expansion is factored once as neg_apply_smul_sub for both the ISR and FSR results, and the pre-existing frame-specific ElectronMethodData is bridged rather than duplicated. The TrueInvariants/ReconstructedInvariants split is required by roadmap convention 1, so it is not duplication.",
